{"id":"mahabharata-1-051","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":51,"title":"एकपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 51 · Astika asks that the sacrifice end","summary":{"en":"The priests urge the king to wait until Takshaka falls; Indra abandons Takshaka, who is drawn helplessly towards the fire. At that moment Astika claims his boon: that the snake sacrifice cease.","kn":"ತಕ್ಷಕನು ಬೀಳುವವರೆಗೆ ಕಾಯಲು ಋತ್ವಿಜರು ರಾಜನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಇಂದ್ರನು ತಕ್ಷಕನನ್ನು ಕೈಬಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವನು ಅಸಹಾಯಕನಾಗಿ ಅಗ್ನಿಯತ್ತ ಸೆಳೆಯಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಆ ಕ್ಷಣದಲ್ಲಿ ಸರ್ಪಯಾಗ ನಿಲ್ಲಲಿ ಎಂದು ಆಸ್ತೀಕನು ವರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"ऋत्विज राजा से तक्षक के गिरने तक रुकने को कहते हैं; इन्द्र तक्षक को छोड़ देते हैं और वह विवश होकर अग्नि की ओर खिंचता है। उसी क्षण आस्तीक वर माँगते हैं कि सर्पयज्ञ रुक जाए।","te":"తక్షకుడు పడే వరకు ఆగమని ఋత్విక్కులు రాజుకు చెబుతారు; ఇంద్రుడు తక్షకుని విడిచిపెడతాడు, అతడు నిస్సహాయంగా అగ్ని వైపు లాగబడతాడు. ఆ క్షణంలో సర్పయాగం ఆగాలని ఆస్తీకుడు వరం కోరుతాడు.","ta":"தக்ஷகன் விழும் வரை காத்திருக்குமாறு ருத்விக்குகள் மன்னனிடம் சொல்கிறார்கள்; இந்திரன் தக்ஷகனைக் கைவிட, அவன் வேறு வழியின்றித் தீயை நோக்கி இழுக்கப்படுகிறான். அக்கணத்தில் ஸர்ப்ப யாகம் நிற்க வேண்டும் என்று ஆஸ்தீகர் வரம் கேட்கிறார்.","ml":"പുരോഹിതന്മാർ തക്ഷകൻ വീഴുന്നതുവരെ കാത്തിരിക്കാൻ രാജാവിനോട് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; ഇന്ദ്രൻ തക്ഷകനെ കൈവിടുന്നു, അദ്ദേഹം നിസ്സഹായനായി അഗ്നിയിലേക്ക് വലിച്ചടുക്കപ്പെടുന്നു. ആ നിമിഷത്തിൽ ആസ്തികൻ തന്റെ വരം ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു: സർപ്പയജ്ഞം നിർത്തണം."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.51; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"बालो वाक्यं स्थविर इव प्रभाषते\nनायं बालः स्थविरोऽयं मतो मे ।\nइच्छाम्यहं वरमस्मै प्रदातुं\nतन्मे विप्रा वितरध्वं समेताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This boy speaks like an elder. I do not consider him a boy but an elder. I want to give him a boon; brahmins, grant me your agreement together."}},{"text":"सदस्या ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The assembly members said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"बालोऽपि विप्रो मान्य एवेह राज्ञां\nयश्चाविद्वान्यश्च विद्वान्यथावत् ।\nसर्वान्कामांस्त्वत्त एषोऽर्हतेऽद्य\nयथा च नस्तक्षक एति शीघ्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin, even a boy, is to be honored by kings, whether unlearned or properly learned. He deserves from you today all that he may desire, provided Takshaka comes to us soon."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"व्याहर्तुकामे वरदे नृपे द्विजं\nवरं वृणीष्वेति ततोऽभ्युवाच ।\nहोता वाक्यं नातिहृष्टान्तरात्मा\nकर्मण्यस्मिंस्तक्षको नैति तावत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king, a giver of boons, was about to speak, he told the brahmin, \"Choose a boon.\" But the Hotri priest, not at all pleased at heart, said: \"In this rite Takshaka has not yet come.\""}},{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"यथा चेदं कर्म समाप्यते मे\nयथा च नस्तक्षक एति शीघ्रम् ।\nतथा भवन्तः प्रयतन्तु सर्वे\nपरं शक्त्या स हि मे विद्विषाणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let all of you strive with your utmost power so that this rite is completed for me and Takshaka comes to us soon, for he is my enemy."}},{"text":"ऋत्विज ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The priests said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"यथा शास्त्राणि नः प्राहुर्यथा शंसति पावकः ।\nइन्द्रस्य भवने राजंस्तक्षको भयपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the scriptures tell us and as the fire declares, king, Takshaka is tormented by fear in Indra's palace."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"यथा सूतो लोहिताक्षो महात्मा\nपौराणिको वेदितवान्पुरस्तात् ।\nस राजानं प्राह पृष्टस्तदानीं\nयथाहुर्विप्रास्तद्वदेतन्नृदेव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled Suta Lohitaksha, who knew the Puranas, had earlier known this, and when asked, told the king just what the brahmins had said, king."}},{"n":7,"text":"पुराणमागम्य ततो ब्रवीम्यहं\nदत्तं तस्मै वरमिन्द्रेण राजन् ।\nवसेह त्वं मत्सकाशे सुगुप्तो\nन पावकस्त्वां प्रदहिष्यतीति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having drawn on the Purana, I say: Indra has given him a boon. 'Stay here with me, well hidden; the fire will not burn you.'\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा दीक्षितस्तप्यमान\nआस्ते होतारं चोदयन्कर्मकाले ।\nहोता च यत्तः स जुहाव मन्त्रै-\nरथो इन्द्रः स्वयमेवाजगाम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, the consecrated king, grieving, urged the Hotri at the time of the rite. The Hotri, striving, made the offering with mantras, and then Indra himself came."}},{"n":9,"text":"विमानमारुह्य महानुभावः\nसर्वैर्देवैः परिसंस्तूयमानः ।\nबलाहकैश्चाप्यनुगम्यमानो\nविद्याधरैरप्सरसां गणैश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Indra, mounted on his aerial car, praised by all the gods, followed by clouds, Vidyadharas and troops of apsarases, arrived."}},{"n":10,"text":"तस्योत्तरीये निहितः स नागो\nभयोद्विग्नः शर्म नैवाभ्यगच्छत् ।\nततो राजा मन्त्रविदोऽब्रवीत्पुनः\nक्रुद्धो वाक्यं तक्षकस्यान्तमिच्छन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The serpent was hidden in the fold of Indra's upper garment, shaken by fear and finding no comfort. Then the king, angry and wishing Takshaka's end, spoke again to those who knew the mantras."}},{"n":11,"text":"इन्द्रस्य भवने विप्रा यदि नागः स तक्षकः ।\nतमिन्द्रेणैव सहितं पातयध्वं विभावसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmins, if the serpent Takshaka is in Indra's palace, then make him fall into the fire, together with Indra himself.\""}},{"text":"ऋत्विज ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The priests said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"अयमायाति वै तूर्णं तक्षकस्ते वशं नृप ।\nश्रूयतेऽस्य महान्नादो रुवतो भैरवं भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Takshaka is coming quickly into your power, king. His loud cry, terrible with fear, is heard as he wails."}},{"n":13,"text":"नूनं मुक्तो वज्रभृता स नागो\nभ्रष्टश्चाङ्कान्मन्त्रविस्रस्तकायः ।\nघूर्णन्नाकाशे नष्टसंज्ञोऽभ्युपैति\nतीव्रान्निःश्वासान्निःश्वसन्पन्नगेन्द्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely the thunderbolt-bearer has let go of that serpent, and he has slipped from Indra's lap with his body loosened by the mantra. Reeling through the sky, senseless, the lord of serpents comes, drawing hard breaths."}},{"n":14,"text":"वर्तते तव राजेन्द्र कर्मैतद्विधिवत्प्रभो ।\nअस्मै तु द्विजमुख्याय वरं त्वं दातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your rite, king of kings, is proceeding as ordained. You should now give a boon to this chief of brahmins."}},{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"बालाभिरूपस्य तवाप्रमेय\nवरं प्रयच्छामि यथानुरूपम् ।\nवृणीष्व यत्तेऽभिमतं हृदि स्थितं\nतत्ते प्रदास्याम्यपि चेददेयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Immeasurable one, I will give a boon as fits you, though you look a boy. Choose what you desire, what lies in your heart; I will give it to you even if it is hard to give."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"पतिष्यमाणे नागेन्द्रे तक्षके जातवेदसि ।\nइदमन्तरमित्येवं तदास्तीकोऽभ्यचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Takshaka, lord of serpents, was falling toward the fire, Astika, seeing this was the moment, urged his request."}},{"n":17,"text":"वरं ददासि चेन्मह्यं वृणोमि जनमेजय ।\nसत्रं ते विरमत्वेतन्न पतेयुरिहोरगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you give me a boon, Janamejaya, I choose this: let your sacrifice stop, and let no more serpents fall into it.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"एवमुक्तस्ततो राजा ब्रह्मन्पारिक्षितस्तदा ।\nनातिहृष्टमना वाक्यमास्तीकमिदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this, Parikshit's son, the king, brahmin, not at all pleased in mind, said these words to Astika."}},{"n":19,"text":"सुवर्णं रजतं गाश्च यच्चान्यन्मन्यसे विभो ।\nतत्ते दद्यां वरं विप्र न निवर्तेत्क्रतुर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Gold, silver, cows, whatever else you think of, lord, I would give you as the boon, brahmin; but do not ask that my sacrifice stop.\""}},{"text":"आस्तीक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Astika said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"सुवर्णं रजतं गाश्च न त्वां राजन्वृणोम्यहम् ।\nसत्रं ते विरमत्वेतत्स्वस्ति मातृकुलस्य नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Gold, silver and cows I do not choose from you, king. Let this sacrifice of yours stop, for the welfare of my mother's family.\""}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"आस्तीकेनैवमुक्तस्तु राजा पारिक्षितस्तदा ।\nपुनः पुनरुवाचेदमास्तीकं वदतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this by Astika, King Janamejaya spoke again and again to Astika, the best of speakers."}},{"n":22,"text":"अन्यं वरय भद्रं ते वरं द्विजवरोत्तम ।\nअयाचत न चाप्यन्यं वरं स भृगुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Choose another boon, best of excellent brahmins; good fortune to you.\" But he, descendant of Bhrigu, asked for no other boon."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो वेदविदस्तत्र सदस्याः सर्व एव तम् ।\nराजानमूचुः सहिता लभतां ब्राह्मणो वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the assembly members, knowers of the Veda, said together to the king: \"Let the brahmin have his boon.\""}}]}]}